{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Correction to the previous comment: one word was lost to shell backtick substitution when I\nposted it. The sentence should read \"...which points at the `declined` counter rather than at\nlog capture\" — the identifier is `declined`, the local counter in\n`apply_inbound_records._inbound_update_apply_links` that guards the once-per-pass summary at\n`apply_inbound_records.py:788` (`if declined:`). Nothing else in that comment was affected.\n\nMy own process note: I passed that comment body as a double-quoted shell argument, so every\nbackticked identifier in it was executed as a command substitution. Any backtick-quoted symbol\nname in a `rebar comment` written that way is silently replaced by the output of running it —\nusually empty. Comment bodies with code identifiers go through a heredoc or a file from here\non, which is how this one was written."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786612798055971001,"uuid":"f3b517f1-9988-4eda-92f3-3ee88d9e3fc3"}